meta {
  name: Webhook Lead Intake (Zapier/FB)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/intake/webhook
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-api-key: {{webhookApiKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "org_id": "{{orgId}}",
    "first_name": "Webhook Lead",
    "last_name": "Test",
    "email": "webhook@example.com",
    "phone": "9998887777",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "source": "facebook",
    "campaign_id": "{{campaignId}}",
    "meta_campaign_id": "23851234567890123",
    "meta_campaign_name": "HIR_Gurugram_Trainer_Sep26",
    "meta_platform": "fb",
    "campaign_type_id": "{{campaignTypeId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Routing fields (1.49.0):

  campaign_type_id -- the POOL this lead routes to, resolved by
  meta-conversion-api, which owns the ext.meta_campaigns mapping. leads-service
  never reads ext.* itself. Absent, it falls back to default_campaign_type_id
  (the page/form default, also passed in) and then to the tenant's is_default
  type. A type belonging to another tenant is a 400, never silently swapped for
  the default.

  meta_campaign_id -- a STRING of digits, not a number: Meta campaign ids run
  past Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER. On first sight of one, leads-service creates
  this branch's marketing.ad_campaigns projection carrying the type.

  When no eligible user exists in the (branch x type) pool, the lead is still
  created, lands unassigned, and leads-service logs lead.autoassign_skipped with
  { org_id, campaign_type, reason }. It does NOT fall back to another pool.
}
